{"text": "Human development is now increasingly understood. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> As an ongoing, flexible, and evolving process. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Rather than a fixed sequence of stages. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> At the core of this perspective. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Lies the concept of plasticity. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Plasticity refers to the human capacity. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To change, adapt, and reorganize cognitive, emotional, and behavioural patterns. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In response to life experiences. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Environmental demands, and biological changes. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It highlights. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That individuals are not merely passive recipients of development. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But active agents capable of growth throughout their lives. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In earlier views. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Development was believed to occur mainly during childhood. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> With adulthood seen as a period of stability. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And old age as a phase of decline. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The concept of plasticity challenges this rigid outlook. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> By emphasizing. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That development continues across the entire lifespan. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Although the extent of change may vary. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> At different stages. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Every phase of life allows. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Room for adaptation and transformation.", "alignment": {"characters": ["H", "u", "m", "a", "n", " ", "d", "e", "v", "e", "l", "o", "p", "m", "e", "n", "t", " ", "i", "s", " ", "n", "o", "w", " ", "i", "n", "c", "r", "e", "a", "s", "i", "n", "g", "l", "y", " ", "u", "n", "d", "e", "r", "s", "t", "o", "o", "d", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "A", "s", " ", "a", "n", " ", "o", "n", "g", "o", "i", "n", "g", ",", " ", "f", "l", "e", "x", "i", "b", "l"